# Background jobs

- Pass record IDs and simple scalar values. Reload records in the worker.
- Make retries safe and idempotent.
- Distinguish terminal failures from retriable failures.
- Enqueue after the database commit unless the transaction boundary is deliberate and documented.
- If required enqueueing fails, move the domain record to an explicit failure state and return an appropriate error.
- Add timeouts, error handling, retry rules, and safe failure states for external API calls.
- Chunk, batch, or fan out long work when one job would be fragile.
- Persist the user-facing write before best-effort notifications.
- Make status and failure information visible to users and operators.
